abstract: >-
  Tests that a HANK code must pass at limits with known answers or at exact identities (permanent-income
  household-block limit, TANK benchmark with imposed incidence, Werning (2015) vanishing liquidity,
  Aiyagari no-idiosyncratic-risk limit, intertemporal Keynesian cross consistency, HANK - RANK differencing
  identity), reported as errors and observed convergence orders rather than single pass/fail checks. Reference implementation on sequence-jacobian 1.0.0, with minimal
  reproductions of two observations about that library (F1, F2). Developed with extensive assistance
  from Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) and reviewed with GPT 6.1 Sol (OpenAI); the author directed and reviewed
  the work and is responsible for the content. See the AI usage disclosure in the README.
keywords:
